That's a suicide mission.

262
00:28:49,825 --> 00:28:53,192
Do yourself a favor, go home.
Live a little longer.

263
00:28:53,362 --> 00:28:58,026
- Dumbledore was confident that he would.
- Do you think he was trustworthy?

264
00:28:58,434 --> 00:29:00,994
Why do you think you can believe him?

265
00:29:01,170 --> 00:29:04,936
In all the time you knew him,
mentioned my name?

266
00:29:05,908 --> 00:29:08,035
Did he mention her name?

267
00:29:08,210 --> 00:29:11,907
- Why would I...?
-Keep secrets? You tell me.

268
00:29:12,915 --> 00:29:16,407
- I trusted him.
- That's a guy's answer.

269
00:29:16,585 --> 00:29:19,679
From a boy who looks for horcruxes
by order of a man...

270
00:29:19,855 --> 00:29:22,585
...who didn't even tell him where
start! You lie!

271
00:29:23,259 --> 00:29:27,059
Not just me, that doesn't matter,
also to yourself.

272
00:29:27,229 --> 00:29:29,254
That's what fools do.

273
00:29:29,431 --> 00:29:33,333
You don't look stupid,
Harry Potter.

274
00:29:33,502 --> 00:29:38,166
So I'll ask you again.
There must be a reason.

275
00:29:40,209 --> 00:29:43,508
I don't care what happened
between you and your brother.

276
00:29:44,213 --> 00:29:46,477
Nor that you have given up.

277
00:29:48,918 --> 00:29:51,546
I trusted
the man I knew.

278
00:29:54,657 --> 00:29:57,751
We need to get into
the castle tonight.

279
00:30:02,998 --> 00:30:05,432
You know what to do.

280
00:30:12,041 --> 00:30:13,975
Where did you send her?

281
00:30:14,443 --> 00:30:18,004
You'll see, very soon.

282
00:30:24,219 --> 00:30:26,983
That's your sister Ariana, right?

283
00:30:27,823 --> 00:30:30,690
He died very young, right?

284
00:30:31,627 --> 00:30:35,358
My brother sacrificed
many things, Mr. Potter...

285
00:30:35,531 --> 00:30:38,022
...in his quest for power...

286
00:30:38,200 --> 00:30:40,464
...including Ariana.

287
00:30:40,869 --> 00:30:43,770
And she was very devoted to him.

288
00:30:44,373 --> 00:30:46,807
He gave her everything...

289
00:30:47,776 --> 00:30:49,505
...except time.

290
00:30:50,879 --> 00:30:53,279
Thank you, Mr. Dumbledore.

291
00:31:00,122 --> 00:31:02,647
He saved our lives twice.

292
00:31:03,292 --> 00:31:05,453
He watched us with that mirror.

293
00:31:06,695 --> 00:31:09,755
Doesn't look like someone
that he has surrendered.

294
00:31:14,937 --> 00:31:17,030
He's coming back.

295
00:31:17,806 --> 00:31:19,899
Who is coming with her?

296
00:31:27,182 --> 00:31:28,240
Neville!

297
00:31:28,417 --> 00:31:30,942
- You look...
- Badly, I guess.

298
00:31:31,120 --> 00:31:33,714
This is nothing.
Seamus is worse.

299
00:31:34,323 --> 00:31:37,918
Hey Ab, a couple are coming
of them more.

300
00:31:39,094 --> 00:31:40,994
I don't remember this about the map.

301
00:31:41,163 --> 00:31:43,063
It hadn't existed until now.

302
00:31:43,232 --> 00:31:46,497
The seven secret passages
They were closed.

303
00:31:46,668 --> 00:31:48,431
You can only enter
or go out here.

304
00:31:48,604 --> 00:31:51,232
It's full of death eaters
and dementors.

305
00:31:51,407 --> 00:31:53,136
How's everything with Snapes?
of director?

306
00:31:53,308 --> 00:31:56,243
We almost never see it.
But be careful with the Carrows.

307
00:31:56,412 --> 00:31:57,436
The Carrows?

308
00:31:57,613 --> 00:32:00,081
Yes. They are brothers and they are in charge
of discipline.

309
00:32:00,249 --> 00:32:01,944
To the Carrows
They love to punish.

310
00:32:02,117 --> 00:32:04,142
Did they do that to you? Because?

311
00:32:04,319 --> 00:32:07,982
They made us practice
the Cruciatus curse.

312
00:32:08,157 --> 00:32:10,057
In first year students.

313
00:32:10,225 --> 00:32:12,056
I refused.

314
00:32:12,861 --> 00:32:14,988
Hogwarts has changed.

315
00:32:27,876 --> 00:32:30,344
Let's have some fun.

316
00:32:35,451 --> 00:32:38,386
Hey!
I brought you a surprise!

317
00:32:38,554 --> 00:32:42,650
I hope it's not more food
Aberforth. It is impossible to digest it.

318
00:32:45,494 --> 00:32:46,586
Heavens!

319
00:33:01,777 --> 00:33:04,610
Tell Remus and the others
that Harry is back.

320
00:33:04,780 --> 00:33:06,941
You don't have to kill him
before You-Know-Who.

321
00:33:07,116 --> 00:33:08,640
Rio, call D.A.

322
00:33:08,817 --> 00:33:11,843
New weather report.
Lightning struck.

323
00:33:12,020 --> 00:33:13,681
What is the plan?

324
00:33:20,562 --> 00:33:22,655
We need to look for something.

325
00:33:22,831 --> 00:33:27,791
It's hidden in the castle.
It will help us against You-Know-Who.

326
00:33:27,970 --> 00:33:29,767
What is it about?

327
00:33:29,938 --> 00:33:31,098
We don't know.

328
00:33:33,075 --> 00:33:35,976
- Where is it?
- We don't know either.

329
00:33:37,346 --> 00:33:40,577
- I know there aren't many clues.
- It's not even a clue.

330
00:33:40,749 --> 00:33:43,513
It has something to do with Ravenclaw.

331
00:33:43,685 --> 00:33:48,054
It's small, easy to hide.

332
00:33:48,924 --> 00:33:51,051
Do you have any ideas?

333
00:33:52,394 --> 00:33:54,885
The diadem is lost
by Rowena Ravenclaw.

334
00:33:55,063 --> 00:33:57,463
Wow, we're starting.

335
00:33:57,633 --> 00:33:59,692
The lost diadem
from Ravenclaw?

336
00:34:00,369 --> 00:34:04,135
Haven't you heard of her?
It is very famous.

337
00:34:04,306 --> 00:34:07,673
Yes, Luna, but it has been lost for centuries.

338
00:34:07,843 --> 00:34:10,641
There is not a single person alive
that he has seen her.

339
00:34:10,812 --> 00:34:13,007
Can you tell me
what is a headband?

340
00:34:13,182 --> 00:34:15,912
It's a kind of crown,
like a tiara.

341
00:34:19,188 --> 00:34:20,450
Harry!

342
00:34:21,723 --> 00:34:23,020
Hello.

343
00:34:26,195 --> 00:34:29,255
Six months without seeing me
and treats me like nothing.

344
00:34:29,431 --> 00:34:31,194
- I'm your brother.
- One of many.

345
00:34:31,366 --> 00:34:33,664
- There is only one Harry.
- Shut up, Seamus.

346
00:34:33,835 --> 00:34:35,325
What's up, Ginny?

347
00:34:35,504 --> 00:34:39,702
Snape knows. You know what they saw
to Harry in Hogsmeade.

348
00:35:18,947 --> 00:35:24,317
Many are wondering why
I sent for them at this time.

349
00:35:26,788 --> 00:35:30,554
I have been informed that
tonight, earlier...

350
00:35:31,994 --> 00:35:34,258
...they saw Harry Potter
in Hogsmeade.

351
00:35:36,765 --> 00:35:38,357
Now...

352
00:35:38,533 --> 00:35:40,125
...if someone...

353
00:35:41,803 --> 00:35:47,036
...student or teacher,
try to help Mr. Potter...

354
00:35:48,176 --> 00:35:50,303
...will be punished
in a consistent way...

355
00:35:50,479 --> 00:35:54,939
...with severity
of his transgression.

356
00:35:55,117 --> 00:35:57,347
Also...

357
00:35:57,719 --> 00:36:02,383
...anyone I've ever had
knowledge of these events...

358
00:36:03,725 --> 00:36:07,661
...and that he has not reported it...

359
00:36:08,597 --> 00:36:13,159
...will be considered...

360
00:36:13,835 --> 00:36:17,032
...equally guilty.

361
00:36:19,341 --> 00:36:21,172
So...

362
00:36:24,646 --> 00:36:26,739
...if any of those present...

363
00:36:27,215 --> 00:36:33,181
...know the moves
from Mr. Potter tonight...

364
00:36:35,624 --> 00:36:39,492
...I invite you to speak...

365
00:36:43,031 --> 00:36:44,726
...now.

366
00:36:59,381 --> 00:37:03,283
It seems that despite their
detailed defense strategies...

367
00:37:03,452 --> 00:37:06,114
...still has problems
security, director.

368
00:37:09,624 --> 00:37:12,616
And I'm afraid they are
quite extensive.

369
00:37:13,362 --> 00:37:15,455
How dare you stand
instead?

370
00:37:17,065 --> 00:37:19,192
Tell them what happened that night!

371
00:37:19,368 --> 00:37:23,896
How he looked into the eyes of a man
who trusted you and killed you!

372
00:37:24,306 --> 00:37:25,933
Tell them!

373
00:37:50,799 --> 00:37:51,823
Coward!

374
00:38:00,909 --> 00:38:03,377
<i>Harry.</i>

375
00:38:04,479 --> 00:38:05,673
Potter?

376
00:38:40,315 --> 00:38:45,878
<i>I know that many of you
They're going to want to fight.</i>

377
00:38:46,054 --> 00:38:51,082
<i>Some will even think
that fighting is prudent.</i>

378
00:38:51,493 --> 00:38:54,553
<i>But that's crazy.</i>

379
00:38:55,030 --> 00:38:57,863
<i>Give me Harry Potter.</i>

380
00:38:58,834 --> 00:39:02,998
<i>Do it and no one will suffer
any damage.</i>

381
00:39:03,171 --> 00:39:09,101
<i>Give me Harry Potter
and I will leave Hogwarts unharmed.</i>

382
00:39:09,377 --> 00:39:12,312
<i>Give me Harry Potter...</i>

383
00:39:12,481 --> 00:39:16,417
<i>...and they will be rewarded.</i>

384
00:39:16,585 --> 00:39:20,180
<i>You have one hour.</i>

385
00:39:29,931 --> 00:39:31,899
What are you waiting for?

386
00:39:32,067 --> 00:39:33,398
Grab it!

387
00:39:42,344 --> 00:39:44,244
The students are up!

388
00:39:45,046 --> 00:39:47,310
Students!

389
00:39:47,482 --> 00:39:49,040
There are students in the hallway!

390
00:39:49,217 --> 00:39:52,618
They got up on purpose, you idiot!

391
00:39:56,024 --> 00:39:57,048
Excuse me, ma'am.

392
00:39:57,225 --> 00:40:01,127
It turns out, Mr. Filch, that
Your arrival is very timely.

393
00:40:01,296 --> 00:40:03,594
If you do me a favor, I would like...

394
00:40:03,765 --> 00:40:08,259
...take Miss Parkinson
and the rest of Slytherin here.

395
00:40:08,436 --> 00:40:10,836
Where do you want
take them, ma'am?

396
00:40:11,006 --> 00:40:13,770
To the dungeons is fine.

397
00:40:15,877 --> 00:40:18,573
I understand. Come on, come on!

398
00:40:18,747 --> 00:40:22,046
I guess you had a reason
to return. What do you need?

399
00:40:22,217 --> 00:40:24,777
Time, teacher,
everything you can give me.

400
00:40:25,387 --> 00:40:28,948
Do what you need to do.
I will guard the castle.

401
00:40:29,824 --> 00:40:31,416
Potter.

402
00:40:33,328 --> 00:40:35,125
I'm glad to see you.

403
00:40:36,064 --> 00:40:38,396
Likewise, teacher.

404
00:40:39,000 --> 00:40:41,230
keep the lines
of battle, Neville.

405
00:40:52,714 --> 00:40:55,274
Harry. Hermione and me
we were thinking.

406
00:40:55,450 --> 00:40:57,384
It doesn't matter what
Let's find the horcrux.

407
00:40:57,552 --> 00:40:59,679
- What do you mean?
- Unless we can destroy it.

408
00:40:59,854 --> 00:41:01,219
We were thinking...

409
00:41:01,389 --> 00:41:03,880
Ron was thinking.
It was his idea. It's brilliant.

410
00:41:04,059 --> 00:41:07,187
A basilisk tusk
destroyed Riddle's diary.

411
00:41:07,362 --> 00:41:09,523
I think we know
where can there be one.

412
00:41:11,700 --> 00:41:15,431
Take this away. So they can
find me when they return.

413
00:41:15,604 --> 00:41:17,663
- Where are you going?
-To the Ravenclaw common room!

414
00:41:17,839 --> 00:41:19,363
It's a start.

415
00:41:25,447 --> 00:41:27,176
Harry!

416
00:41:29,050 --> 00:41:30,540
Let me see if I understood,
teacher.

417
00:41:30,719 --> 00:41:34,678
- Did you give us permission to do this?
- Right, Longbottom.

418
00:41:34,856 --> 00:41:36,289
To blow it up? Boom?

419
00:41:36,458 --> 00:41:37,948
Boom!

420
00:41:38,126 --> 00:41:41,527
Fantastic.
But how are we going to do it?

421
00:41:41,696 --> 00:41:44,028
Why don't you discuss it?
with Mr. Finnegan?

422
00:41:44,199 --> 00:41:47,760
If I remember correctly,
He is fond of pyrotechnics.

423
00:41:47,936 --> 00:41:48,960
I can knock him down.

424
00:41:49,137 --> 00:41:51,503
Exactly. Now go.

425
00:41:52,374 --> 00:41:55,741
We can't keep out
to You-Know-Who forever.

426
00:41:55,910 --> 00:41:59,073
It doesn't mean that
we cannot delay it.

427
00:41:59,748 --> 00:42:04,242
And his name is Voldemort, Filius.
Use the name once and for all.

428
00:42:04,419 --> 00:42:07,320
He's still going to try to kill you.

429
00:42:09,591 --> 00:42:12,890
<i>Piertotum Locomotor!</i>

430
00:42:28,443 --> 00:42:30,240
Hogwarts is threatened!

431
00:42:30,412 --> 00:42:36,312
Protect the walls! Protect us!
Do your duty!

432
00:42:39,621 --> 00:42:43,352
I had always wanted
use that spell.

433
00:42:52,200 --> 00:42:55,169
<i>I protect Maxima. Fianto Duri.
Repello Inimicum.</i>

434
00:42:55,336 --> 00:42:59,966
<i>I protect Maxima. Fianto Duri.
Repello Inimicum.</i>

435
00:43:00,141 --> 00:43:04,908
<i>I protect Maxima. Fianto Duri.
Repello Inimicum.</i>

436
00:43:05,080 --> 00:43:06,741
<i>I protect Maxima.</i>

437
00:43:34,943 --> 00:43:39,346
-Harry, wait! I need to talk to you.
- I'm a little busy, Luna.

438
00:43:39,514 --> 00:43:42,142
You won't find anything!
You're wasting your time!

439
00:43:42,317 --> 00:43:44,308
We'll talk later, okay?

440
00:43:44,486 --> 00:43:45,885
- Later!
-Harry Potter!

441
00:43:46,054 --> 00:43:47,988
Listen to me right now!

442
00:43:49,491 --> 00:43:52,551
Do you remember what Cho said
of the Ravenclaw diadem?

443
00:43:53,027 --> 00:43:55,962
"No person alive
has seen her."

444
00:43:56,131 --> 00:44:00,830
It's obvious, right? we have to talk
with someone who is dead.

445
00:44:11,212 --> 00:44:14,010
It's impressive, isn't it?

446
00:44:29,364 --> 00:44:31,992
If it's anywhere, it's down there.

447
00:44:32,167 --> 00:44:33,600
Aren't you coming?

448
00:44:33,768 --> 00:44:36,259
It's better that they talk to themselves.

449
00:44:36,437 --> 00:44:38,632
She is very shy.

450
00:45:05,166 --> 00:45:06,690
You are the Gray Lady...

451
00:45:07,468 --> 00:45:09,231
...the Ghost in the Tower
from Ravenclaw.

452
00:45:09,404 --> 00:45:11,133
I don't answer to that name.

453
00:45:11,306 --> 00:45:15,868
No, sorry. Your name is Helena, right?
Helena Ravenclaw.

454
00:45:16,044 --> 00:45:18,171
Rowena's daughter.

455
00:45:18,346 --> 00:45:20,371
Are you Luna's friend?

456
00:45:20,548 --> 00:45:22,482
Yes.

457
00:45:22,650 --> 00:45:25,118
She thinks you can help me.

458
00:45:27,021 --> 00:45:29,615
You're looking for my mother's diadem.

459
00:45:31,125 --> 00:45:32,820
Yes.

460
00:45:33,728 --> 00:45:34,786
That's right.

461
00:45:36,531 --> 00:45:41,195
Luna is kind,
unlike many others.

462
00:45:41,369 --> 00:45:44,429
But I was wrong.
I can't help you.

463
00:45:49,077 --> 00:45:51,511
Wait, please!

464
00:45:53,214 --> 00:45:55,239
I want to destroy it!

465
00:46:33,254 --> 00:46:35,745
They never learn.

466
00:46:36,858 --> 00:46:38,917
What a pity.

467
00:46:39,193 --> 00:46:42,526
But, my lord...

468
00:46:42,697 --> 00:46:44,961
...shouldn't we wait for...?

469
00:46:45,133 --> 00:46:46,862
My lord.

470
00:46:52,040 --> 00:46:53,507
Start.

471
00:47:14,128 --> 00:47:16,460
It's what you want
you too, right?

472
00:47:22,036 --> 00:47:23,298
You want to destroy it.

473
00:47:23,471 --> 00:47:26,497
Another person swore to destroy it
many years ago...

474
00:47:26,674 --> 00:47:29,541
...a strange child
with a strange name.

475
00:47:29,711 --> 00:47:32,544
-Tom Riddle.
- But he lied.

476
00:47:32,714 --> 00:47:33,874
He has lied to many.

477
00:47:34,048 --> 00:47:37,176
I know what he has done!
I know who it is!

478
00:47:37,352 --> 00:47:40,253
He corrupted her with dark magic!

479
00:47:55,236 --> 00:47:58,933
I can destroy it
once and for all.

480
00:48:00,908 --> 00:48:03,877
But only if you tell me
where he hid it.

481
00:48:05,847 --> 00:48:11,615
You know where he hid it,
right, Helena?

482
00:48:13,154 --> 00:48:15,622
You just need to tell me.

483
00:48:17,125 --> 00:48:18,888
Please.

484
00:48:30,638 --> 00:48:32,936
How strange.

485
00:48:35,810 --> 00:48:38,904
You remind me a little of him.

486
00:48:40,114 --> 00:48:41,376
It's here...

487
00:48:42,050 --> 00:48:46,316
...in the castle, in the place
where everything is hidden.

488
00:48:48,523 --> 00:48:49,922
If you have to ask...

489
00:48:50,091 --> 00:48:52,389
...you will never know.

490
00:48:53,394 --> 00:48:57,330
If you know,
you just need to ask.

491
00:48:58,499 --> 00:49:00,194
Thank you.

492
00:49:12,947 --> 00:49:17,247
Tell Professor McGonagall that
Remus and I will defend this side.

493
00:49:18,086 --> 00:49:19,815
Yes, sir.

494
00:49:23,224 --> 00:49:26,352
Dean, on second thought,
tell the teacher...

495
00:49:26,527 --> 00:49:29,325
...which we may need
one or two more wands.

496
00:49:31,833 --> 00:49:34,825
The quality of your convictions
determines success...

497
00:49:35,002 --> 00:49:36,765
...not the number of followers.

498
00:49:36,938 --> 00:49:38,929
Who said that?

499
00:49:39,373 --> 00:49:40,931
I.

500
00:49:45,680 --> 00:49:47,614
Are you okay, Freddie?

501
00:49:47,982 --> 00:49:49,415
Yes.

502
00:49:50,885 --> 00:49:52,580
Me too.

503
00:50:09,670 --> 00:50:13,299
Harry talks in his sleep.
Have you noticed?

504
00:50:14,175 --> 00:50:16,200
No, of course not.

505
00:51:03,791 --> 00:51:05,418
Yes?

506
00:51:05,593 --> 00:51:07,083
Do you and whose army?

507
00:51:27,281 --> 00:51:28,942
- Do it.
- Can't.

508
00:51:29,116 --> 00:51:31,209
Yes, yes you can.

509
00:54:29,296 --> 00:54:30,923
Neville!

510
00:54:48,115 --> 00:54:50,015
It turned out well.

511
00:55:36,163 --> 00:55:40,224
Get in! Everyone cover up!

512
00:55:57,918 --> 00:55:59,715
<i>Fainting!</i>

513
00:56:02,756 --> 00:56:05,850
Ginny! Neville!
Are you guys okay?

514
00:56:06,026 --> 00:56:10,554
Better than ever! I feel like I can
spit fire! Have you seen Luna?

515
00:56:10,731 --> 00:56:12,562
- To Luna?
- I'm crazy about her!

516
00:56:12,733 --> 00:56:17,033
I have to tell you,
Because we might not survive!

517
00:56:21,008 --> 00:56:22,771
I already know.

518
00:56:50,571 --> 00:56:53,165
We never go
to find in this.

519
00:56:53,340 --> 00:56:56,002
- There it is, right there.
- Fantastic.

520
00:56:56,176 --> 00:57:00,044
Disappeared.
In this moment. I saw it.

521
00:57:02,616 --> 00:57:04,584
Maybe he went to the Room of Requirement.

522
00:57:04,752 --> 00:57:08,210
It's not on the map.
You said it last year.

523
00:57:08,389 --> 00:57:10,721
It's true, that's what I said.

524
00:57:10,891 --> 00:57:12,586
Let's go there.

525
00:57:13,294 --> 00:57:15,023
Great.

526
00:57:20,634 --> 00:57:22,295
Come!

527
00:59:14,214 --> 00:59:15,545
Wow, wow.

528
00:59:16,517 --> 00:59:18,576
What brings you here?

529
00:59:19,420 --> 00:59:21,285
I'm asking you the same thing.

530
00:59:21,889 --> 00:59:23,948
You have something of mine.

531
00:59:24,825 --> 00:59:26,349
I want you to give it back to me.

532
00:59:26,527 --> 00:59:28,893
- What's wrong with that one?
- It's my mother's.

533
00:59:29,063 --> 00:59:32,931
It is powerful,
but it's not the same.

534
00:59:33,100 --> 00:59:36,729
He doesn't completely understand me.

535
00:59:37,237 --> 00:59:38,704
Do you understand me?

536
00:59:39,306 --> 00:59:41,240
Why didn't you tell him?

537
00:59:42,910 --> 00:59:44,104
To Bellatrix.

538
00:59:47,514 --> 00:59:49,448
You knew it was me.

539
00:59:50,184 --> 00:59:51,708
You didn't tell him anything.

540
00:59:51,885 --> 00:59:53,750
Come on, Draco.

541
00:59:53,921 --> 00:59:57,084
Don't be stupid. Kill him.

542
00:59:57,891 --> 00:59:59,222
Quiet.

543
01:00:00,627 --> 01:00:01,924
<i>Expelliarmus!</i>

544
01:00:02,096 --> 01:00:03,120
<i>Avada Kedavra!</i>

545
01:00:03,297 --> 01:00:04,321
<i>Fainting!</i>

546
01:00:08,535 --> 01:00:11,834
She's my girlfriend, you idiots!

547
01:00:33,427 --> 01:00:35,054
I got it!

548
01:00:41,835 --> 01:00:43,200
Run!

549
01:00:44,438 --> 01:00:45,632
Run!

550
01:00:49,676 --> 01:00:52,543
Goyle is on fire
the damn place!

551
01:01:59,546 --> 01:02:01,446
Follow me! Here!

552
01:02:08,755 --> 01:02:10,746
We can't leave them!

553
01:02:10,924 --> 01:02:13,085
You're joking, right?

554
01:02:21,768 --> 01:02:24,601
If we die for them,
Harry, I'll kill you!

555
01:02:47,294 --> 01:02:48,955
Harry!

556
01:03:35,409 --> 01:03:36,706
My lord?

557
01:03:36,877 --> 01:03:39,402
<i>Avada Kedavra!</i>

558
01:03:45,752 --> 01:03:50,018
Come, Nagini.
I have to keep you safe.

559
01:04:02,402 --> 01:04:04,233
It's the snake.

560
01:04:04,404 --> 01:04:07,999
She is the last one,
the last horcrux.

561
01:04:14,681 --> 01:04:17,081
Look inside him, Harry.

562
01:04:17,250 --> 01:04:21,016
Find out where it is. If we find it,
we found the snake...

563
01:04:21,188 --> 01:04:23,315
...and we can finish this.

564
01:04:51,018 --> 01:04:52,747
My lord?

565
01:04:52,919 --> 01:04:56,787
Wouldn't it be less...

566
01:04:57,557 --> 01:05:01,857
Wouldn't it be more prudent
cancel this attack...

567
01:05:02,329 --> 01:05:04,923
...and that you would look for the boy?

568
01:05:05,098 --> 01:05:08,431
I don't need to look for the boy.

569
01:05:08,602 --> 01:05:13,005
Before the night is over,
he will come to me! You understand?

570
01:05:14,941 --> 01:05:16,932
Look at me!

571
01:05:17,110 --> 01:05:21,069
How can you live
With yourself, Lucius?

572
01:05:21,248 --> 01:05:23,011
I don't know.

573
01:05:25,118 --> 01:05:27,643
Find Severus.

574
01:05:28,255 --> 01:05:30,314
Bring it to me.

575
01:05:38,331 --> 01:05:40,356
I already know where it is.

576
01:05:50,043 --> 01:05:52,136
Come!

577
01:06:32,185 --> 01:06:34,312
<i>Crucio!</i>

578
01:06:40,060 --> 01:06:41,493
Nope!

579
01:07:27,641 --> 01:07:30,872
you have done extraordinary magic
with that wand...

580
01:07:31,044 --> 01:07:33,069
...and that's just in the last few hours.

581
01:07:33,246 --> 01:07:35,009
No.

582
01:07:35,482 --> 01:07:38,747
No, I am extraordinary...

583
01:07:38,919 --> 01:07:42,548
...but the wand resists me.

584
01:07:42,722 --> 01:07:45,782
There is no more powerful wand.

585
01:07:45,959 --> 01:07:48,757
Ollivander himself said it.

586
01:07:48,929 --> 01:07:54,561
Tonight, when the boy comes,
will not fail you. I'm sure.

587
01:07:56,603 --> 01:07:59,436
He answers to you...

588
01:08:00,307 --> 01:08:02,639
...and only you.

589
01:08:03,376 --> 01:08:04,866
Really?

590
01:08:07,869 --> 01:08:09,393
My lord?

591
01:08:11,706 --> 01:08:16,040
The wand.
Are you really answering me?

592
01:08:17,812 --> 01:08:19,905
You're a smart man, Severus.

593
01:08:20,081 --> 01:08:21,981
Surely you must know.

594
01:08:23,685 --> 01:08:27,382
Who do you deposit with?
his true loyalty?

595
01:08:27,889 --> 01:08:29,652
In you...

596
01:08:30,158 --> 01:08:32,251
...of course, my lord.

597
01:08:32,427 --> 01:08:33,621
The Elder Wand...

598
01:08:34,429 --> 01:08:40,231
...it can't help me because
I am not his true master.

599
01:08:41,336 --> 01:08:46,831
The Elder Wand belongs to him
to the magician who killed its last owner.

600
01:08:52,747 --> 01:08:56,410
You killed Dumbledore, Severus.

601
01:08:57,285 --> 01:09:02,552
While you live, the Elder Wand
It cannot be truly mine.

602
01:09:04,025 --> 01:09:07,756
You have been a servant
good and loyal, Severus...

603
01:09:08,263 --> 01:09:13,326
...but only I can
live forever.

604
01:09:16,638 --> 01:09:17,662
My lord...

605
01:09:23,678 --> 01:09:25,771
Nagini, kill!

606
01:10:26,574 --> 01:10:28,542
Pick them up.

607
01:10:29,711 --> 01:10:31,645
Pick them up.

608
01:10:32,480 --> 01:10:33,947
Please.

609
01:10:34,115 --> 01:10:37,812
Give me something. Soon!
A jar, anything!

610
01:10:56,137 --> 01:10:57,604
Take them to the Pensieve.

611
01:11:01,176 --> 01:11:03,144
Look at me.

612
01:11:08,883 --> 01:11:11,613
You have your mother's eyes.

613
01:11:45,286 --> 01:11:48,847
<i>They have fought bravely...</i>

614
01:11:50,258 --> 01:11:52,988
<i>...but in vain.</i>

615
01:11:56,297 --> 01:11:58,561
<i>I do not want this.</i>

616
01:11:58,733 --> 01:12:04,262
<i>Every drop of magical blood spilled
It's a terrible waste.</i>

617
01:12:04,439 --> 01:12:09,206
<i>Therefore, I command you
to my forces to withdraw.</i>

618
01:12:09,377 --> 01:12:14,906
<i>In his absence, get rid of
of their dead with dignity.</i>

619
01:12:15,416 --> 01:12:21,346
<i>Harry Potter, now
I speak directly to you.</i>

620
01:12:21,623 --> 01:12:26,993
<i>Tonight you allowed
your friends would die for you...</i>

621
01:12:27,162 --> 01:12:29,653
<i>...instead of facing me yourself.</i>

622
01:12:29,831 --> 01:12:33,392
<i>There is no greater disgrace.</i>

623
01:12:33,568 --> 01:12:38,528
<i>Catch me in the Forbidden Forest
and confront your destiny.</i>

624
01:12:39,774 --> 01:12:42,368
<i>If you don't...</i>

625
01:12:42,544 --> 01:12:46,894
<i>...I will kill every last man...</i>

626
01:12:46,895 --> 01:12:49,245
<i>...woman and child...</i>

627
01:12:49,417 --> 01:12:53,979
<i>...try to hide you from me.</i>

628
01:13:13,541 --> 01:13:15,475
Where is everyone?

629
01:13:40,268 --> 01:13:41,292
Harry.

630
01:13:46,975 --> 01:13:49,739
Please. What's the matter?

631
01:13:49,911 --> 01:13:51,538
He already left us.

632
01:13:53,348 --> 01:13:55,839
Yes, it left us.

633
01:16:04,579 --> 01:16:05,603
Phenomenon!

634
01:16:05,780 --> 01:16:07,270
Come here!

635
01:16:07,448 --> 01:16:09,507
I'm going to tell mommy!
You are a phenomenon!

636
01:16:09,684 --> 01:16:12,118
You are a phenomenon, Lily!

637
01:16:12,286 --> 01:16:13,878
Come here!

638
01:16:34,876 --> 01:16:38,175
He envies you because he is
ordinary and you are special.

639
01:16:38,346 --> 01:16:40,871
Don't be mean, Severus.

640
01:17:03,704 --> 01:17:06,036
<i>Gryffindor!</i>

641
01:17:13,314 --> 01:17:16,249
- Hello, I'm James.
- I'm Lily.

642
01:17:20,822 --> 01:17:24,952
<i>You are identical to your father.
Lazy, arrogant.</i>

643
01:17:25,126 --> 01:17:26,957
<i>Don't say anything against my father!</i>

644
01:17:33,267 --> 01:17:34,859
<i>Blood will flow...</i>

645
01:17:35,036 --> 01:17:40,030
...and master and servant
They will meet again!

646
01:17:40,208 --> 01:17:42,108
<i>Severus.</i>

647
01:17:43,177 --> 01:17:45,168
Don't kill me!

648
01:17:45,346 --> 01:17:49,180
The prophecy did not mention
to a woman

649
01:17:49,350 --> 01:17:51,614
He was referring to a child
born at the end of July.

650
01:17:51,786 --> 01:17:54,016
He believes he is her son.

651
01:17:54,622 --> 01:17:57,785
has the intention
to hunt them, to kill them.

652
01:17:57,959 --> 01:18:02,453
Hide her, hide them all.
I beg you.

653
01:18:02,630 --> 01:18:05,724
What will you give me in return, Severus?

654
01:18:07,468 --> 01:18:08,492
Whatever you want.

655
01:18:08,669 --> 01:18:13,402
Harry, you are very loved.
Very loved.

656
01:18:14,408 --> 01:18:17,070
Harry, mom loves you.

657
01:18:17,245 --> 01:18:20,146
Daddy loves you.

658
01:18:21,015 --> 01:18:23,176
Harry, take care of yourself.

659
01:18:23,351 --> 01:18:24,375
Be strong.

660
01:18:24,552 --> 01:18:26,042
<i>Avada Kedavra!</i>

661
01:18:30,558 --> 01:18:35,018
You said you were going to protect her.

662
01:18:35,196 --> 01:18:39,223
Lily and James trusted
the wrong person, Severus.

663
01:18:40,201 --> 01:18:42,260
Just like you.

664
01:18:44,405 --> 01:18:45,872
The boy survived.

665
01:18:46,040 --> 01:18:48,304
He's safe.
The Dark Lord is gone.

666
01:18:48,476 --> 01:18:50,706
The Dark Lord will return.

667
01:18:50,878 --> 01:18:54,439
And when I come back,
The child will be in great danger.

668
01:18:55,650 --> 01:18:57,982
He has her eyes.

669
01:19:01,455 --> 01:19:04,618
If you really loved her...

670
01:19:07,328 --> 01:19:11,162
Nobody can find out.

671
01:19:11,332 --> 01:19:13,732
<i>Shouldn't I reveal the best of you?</i>

672
01:19:13,901 --> 01:19:14,959
<i>Give me your word.</i>

673
01:19:15,136 --> 01:19:18,105
<i>When you risk your life
daily to protect the child?</i>

674
01:19:18,272 --> 01:19:21,833
<i>He has no talent, his arrogance
even equals that of his father...</i>

675
01:19:22,009 --> 01:19:23,874
<i>...and savor its fame.</i>

676
01:19:24,045 --> 01:19:26,912
<i>Don't say anything against my father!</i>

677
01:19:27,081 --> 01:19:29,276
<i>James Potter?</i>

678
01:19:29,450 --> 01:19:30,940
<i>Lazy, arrogant.</i>

679
01:19:31,118 --> 01:19:32,449
<i>My father was a great man!</i>

680
01:19:32,620 --> 01:19:34,520
Your father was a pig!

681
01:19:36,357 --> 01:19:38,018
<i>Take the rest.</i>

682
01:19:38,192 --> 01:19:42,219
Will contain damage to your hand
for the moment.

683
01:19:42,396 --> 01:19:44,330
It's going to spread, Albus.

684
01:19:44,498 --> 01:19:46,193
How much time do I have?

685
01:19:47,168 --> 01:19:49,636
Maybe a year.

686
01:19:51,839 --> 01:19:52,999
Don't ignore me, Severus.

687
01:19:53,174 --> 01:19:54,664
<i>Harmonia Nectere Passus.</i>

688
01:19:54,842 --> 01:19:58,801
We both know that Voldemort
He ordered Draco Malfoy to kill me.

689
01:20:00,881 --> 01:20:05,113
But if it fails, we must assume
that the Dark Lord...

690
01:20:05,286 --> 01:20:07,413
...will come to you.

691
01:20:10,157 --> 01:20:14,093
You must be the one
Killed me, Severus.

692
01:20:14,261 --> 01:20:16,422
It's the only way.

693
01:20:17,398 --> 01:20:21,767
Only then the Dark Lord
He will trust you completely.

694
01:20:21,936 --> 01:20:24,598
<i>Avada Kedavra!</i>

695
01:20:27,842 --> 01:20:32,779
<i>The time will come when Harry
Potter must find out something.</i>

696
01:20:34,348 --> 01:20:39,547
You must wait for Voldemort
is at its most vulnerable point.

697
01:20:39,720 --> 01:20:42,621
Should he find out what?

698
01:20:42,790 --> 01:20:48,194
<i>The night that Lord Voldemort was
to Godric's Hollow to kill Harry...</i>

699
01:20:49,196 --> 01:20:51,926
<i>...and Lily Potter stepped in
among them...</i>

700
01:20:52,700 --> 01:20:54,634
<i>...the curse rebounded.</i>

701
01:20:56,437 --> 01:21:00,066
When that happens, a part
of Voldemort's soul...

702
01:21:00,241 --> 01:21:05,076
...got hooked on the one thing
alive that he could find:

703
01:21:05,246 --> 01:21:07,373
<i>To Harry himself.</i>

704
01:21:08,716 --> 01:21:12,152
<i>There's a reason Harry can talk
with the snakes.</i>

705
01:21:12,720 --> 01:21:15,553
<i>For some reason it can enter
in Voldemort's mind.</i>

706
01:21:17,925 --> 01:21:23,889
A part of Voldemort
lives inside him.

707
01:21:30,438 --> 01:21:33,373
So when the time comes...

708
01:21:34,275 --> 01:21:36,436
...must the boy die?

709
01:21:38,345 --> 01:21:40,370
Yes. Yes.

710
01:21:40,548 --> 01:21:42,812
<i>He must die.</i>

711
01:22:01,102 --> 01:22:05,971
You kept him alive so that
would die at the appropriate time.

712
01:22:09,610 --> 01:22:13,205
<i>You raised him like a pig
for the slaughterhouse.</i>

713
01:22:13,380 --> 01:22:17,783
Don't tell me that you
you fell in love with the boy.

714
01:22:22,289 --> 01:22:25,554
<i>Expecto Patronum.</i>

715
01:22:36,470 --> 01:22:37,960
Lily.

716
01:22:41,242 --> 01:22:43,608
<i>After so long?</i>

717
01:22:47,014 --> 01:22:49,141
Always.

718
01:22:54,288 --> 01:22:57,280
<i>So when it comes
the moment...</i>

719
01:22:57,458 --> 01:23:00,450
<i>...must the boy die?</i>

720
01:23:00,628 --> 01:23:03,995
Yes. He must die.

721
01:23:04,165 --> 01:23:07,157
And Voldemort himself
must kill him.

722
01:23:07,601 --> 01:23:09,796
That is essential.

723
01:24:14,869 --> 01:24:15,893
Where were you?

724
01:24:16,070 --> 01:24:19,233
- We believed you in the forest.
- I'm going there.

725
01:24:19,406 --> 01:24:22,375
Are you crazy? No!

726
01:24:23,110 --> 01:24:25,601
You can't give yourself to him.

727
01:24:28,949 --> 01:24:30,849
What do you have, Harry?

728
01:24:32,386 --> 01:24:34,320
What do you know?

729
01:24:37,091 --> 01:24:39,685
There's a reason why
I can hear them.

730
01:24:40,294 --> 01:24:41,522
To the horcruxes.

731
01:24:44,031 --> 01:24:46,397
I think I knew
for a long time.

732
01:24:47,835 --> 01:24:50,099
And I think you do too.

733
01:24:53,073 --> 01:24:56,236
- I'll go with you.
- No, kill the snake.

734
01:24:56,977 --> 01:24:59,104
kill the snake
and only he will remain.

735
01:26:13,787 --> 01:26:16,779
I OPEN TO CLOSING

736
01:26:19,326 --> 01:26:21,351
I'm ready to die.

737
01:27:02,669 --> 01:27:05,103
The Stone of Resurrection.

738
01:27:34,768 --> 01:27:38,169
You have been very brave, sweetheart.

739
01:27:42,242 --> 01:27:44,107
What are they doing here?

740
01:27:44,912 --> 01:27:46,709
All of you?

741
01:27:49,083 --> 01:27:51,244
We never left.

742
01:28:00,127 --> 01:28:01,719
D...?

743
01:28:02,463 --> 01:28:03,657
Does it hurt?

744
01:28:04,698 --> 01:28:06,393
Die?

745
01:28:07,334 --> 01:28:09,859
It's faster than falling asleep.

746
01:28:13,774 --> 01:28:16,072
You're almost there, son.

747
01:28:16,243 --> 01:28:17,437
I'm sorry.

748
01:28:17,611 --> 01:28:21,103
I never wanted anyone
would die for me.

749
01:28:22,716 --> 01:28:24,308
And, Remus, your son...

750
01:28:24,485 --> 01:28:28,751
Others will tell you why
his parents died.

751
01:28:28,922 --> 01:28:32,380
One day you will understand.

752
01:28:44,138 --> 01:28:45,662
Are you going to stay with me?

753
01:28:47,241 --> 01:28:49,505
Until the end.

754
01:28:50,210 --> 01:28:52,178
And he won't be able to see them?

755
01:28:52,346 --> 01:28:54,007
No.

756
01:28:55,315 --> 01:28:57,909
You see, we are here.

757
01:29:12,466 --> 01:29:14,491
Stay close to me.

758
01:29:16,236 --> 01:29:18,397
Always.

759
01:29:33,153 --> 01:29:36,884
There is no trace of him, my lord.

760
01:29:52,339 --> 01:29:55,103
I thought he was going to come.

761
01:30:35,949 --> 01:30:37,041
Harry?

762
01:30:37,217 --> 01:30:39,617
Nope! What are you doing here?

763
01:30:39,786 --> 01:30:41,083
Silence!

764
01:30:52,099 --> 01:30:54,363
Harry Potter.

765
01:30:57,471 --> 01:31:00,167
The boy who lived.

766
01:31:04,411 --> 01:31:06,845
He is coming to die.

767
01:31:25,065 --> 01:31:26,760
<i>Avada Kedavra!</i>

768
01:32:23,457 --> 01:32:24,856
You can't help him.

769
01:32:25,792 --> 01:32:26,816
Harry...

770
01:32:27,427 --> 01:32:29,691
...wonderful boy.

771
01:32:30,197 --> 01:32:34,099
You are a very man,
very brave.

772
01:32:36,069 --> 01:32:38,037
Walk with me.

773
01:32:45,512 --> 01:32:47,742
Professor, what is that?

774
01:32:50,450 --> 01:32:53,476
Something out of reach
of our help.

775
01:32:56,356 --> 01:32:59,621
A part of Voldemort
She was sent here to die.

776
01:32:59,993 --> 01:33:01,187
Where are we exactly?

777
01:33:02,462 --> 01:33:06,421
I was going to ask you that.
Where would you say we are?

778
01:33:06,600 --> 01:33:08,329
Well...

779
01:33:08,502 --> 01:33:11,096
...it looks like King's Cross station.

780
01:33:11,471 --> 01:33:13,769
But cleaner.

781
01:33:13,940 --> 01:33:16,170
And without all the trains.

782
01:33:16,710 --> 01:33:19,440
King's Cross? It's true?

783
01:33:19,813 --> 01:33:23,374
This is, as they say, your party.

784
01:33:24,551 --> 01:33:27,543
Have you realized that
you and Voldemort...

785
01:33:27,721 --> 01:33:30,554
...have been connected
not just because of destiny...

786
01:33:30,724 --> 01:33:33,750
...since that night in the Valley
from Godric years ago.

787
01:33:33,927 --> 01:33:35,656
So is it true, sir?

788
01:33:35,829 --> 01:33:38,798
Does a part of him live
inside me?

789
01:33:39,132 --> 01:33:40,156
He lived.

790
01:33:40,333 --> 01:33:45,134
It was destroyed a few moments ago
by Voldemort himself.

791
01:33:46,206 --> 01:33:50,905
You were the horcrux that
he didn't do it on purpose.

792
01:34:03,457 --> 01:34:05,823
I have to go back, right?

793
01:34:05,992 --> 01:34:07,050
That's up to you.

794
01:34:07,227 --> 01:34:08,990
Can I decide?

795
01:34:09,162 --> 01:34:10,959
Yes.

796
01:34:11,131 --> 01:34:13,964
We're in King's Cross, you say?

797
01:34:15,068 --> 01:34:19,869
I think that if you want
you can board a train.

798
01:34:21,274 --> 01:34:23,367
And where would it take me?

799
01:34:24,177 --> 01:34:26,008
Beyond.

800
01:34:43,997 --> 01:34:46,090
Voldemort has the Elder Wand.

801
01:34:48,735 --> 01:34:49,759
It's true.

802
01:34:49,936 --> 01:34:52,734
- And the snake is still alive.
- Yes.

803
01:34:52,906 --> 01:34:55,466
And I have nothing to kill her with.

804
01:34:56,009 --> 01:35:00,742
Help will always be given
at Hogwarts to those who ask for it.

805
01:35:01,948 --> 01:35:05,645
I have always been proud
of my eloquence.

806
01:35:06,586 --> 01:35:09,714
The words are, in me
not so humble opinion...

807
01:35:09,890 --> 01:35:13,485
...our source more
inexhaustible of magic.

808
01:35:13,660 --> 01:35:17,994
Capable of both inflicting
wounds as well as healing them.

809
01:35:18,632 --> 01:35:24,537
But in this case, I would like
correct my original statement:

810
01:35:27,340 --> 01:35:33,306
Help will always be provided
Hogwarts to those who deserve it.

811
01:35:39,352 --> 01:35:42,116
Don't feel sorry for the dead.

812
01:35:42,556 --> 01:35:44,581
Take pity on the living.

813
01:35:45,158 --> 01:35:50,027
And, more than anything,
of those who live without love.

814
01:35:50,997 --> 01:35:56,401
Professor, the Patronus of
My mother was a deer, right?

815
01:35:57,470 --> 01:36:00,064
Professor Snape has the same one.

816
01:36:00,941 --> 01:36:03,034
It's curious, don't you think?

817
01:36:03,209 --> 01:36:08,169
The truth is, if I think about it,
There is nothing curious about it.

818
01:36:09,883 --> 01:36:12,044
I'm leaving, Harry.

819
01:36:12,586 --> 01:36:13,917
Professor?

820
01:36:18,425 --> 01:36:20,586
Is all this real?

821
01:36:21,261 --> 01:36:23,092
Or is it just happening
inside my head?

822
01:36:23,263 --> 01:36:26,790
Of course it's happening
inside your head, Harry.

823
01:36:26,967 --> 01:36:30,733
Why should it mean
that is not real?

824
01:36:36,309 --> 01:36:37,901
Professor?

825
01:36:38,078 --> 01:36:39,909
What should I do?

826
01:36:43,683 --> 01:36:45,446
Professor?

827
01:36:48,822 --> 01:36:50,119
My lord?

828
01:36:50,290 --> 01:36:52,417
My lord! Are you hurt?

829
01:36:52,592 --> 01:36:54,219
I don't need your help.

830
01:36:54,394 --> 01:36:57,090
No. Come on, get up.

831
01:37:05,805 --> 01:37:07,636
The boy!

832
01:37:07,807 --> 01:37:09,741
Is he dead?

833
01:37:23,823 --> 01:37:26,018
Is he alive?

834
01:37:26,192 --> 01:37:28,387
Draco? Is he alive?

835
01:37:55,055 --> 01:37:56,955
Dead.

836
01:39:23,743 --> 01:39:26,371
Who is that?
Who does Hagrid bring?

837
01:39:27,046 --> 01:39:28,877
Neville, who is this?

838
01:39:29,549 --> 01:39:32,040
Harry Potter...

839
01:39:33,186 --> 01:39:34,676
...has died!

840
01:39:36,589 --> 01:39:37,954
Silence!

841
01:39:41,761 --> 01:39:43,752
Stupid girl!

842
01:39:44,898 --> 01:39:48,334
Harry Potter is dead.

843
01:39:48,501 --> 01:39:53,632
From this day forward,
They will put their faith...

844
01:39:53,807 --> 01:39:54,865
...in me.

845
01:40:05,351 --> 01:40:08,218
Harry Potter is dead!

846
01:40:12,525 --> 01:40:15,983
And this is the time to declare yourself.

847
01:40:17,564 --> 01:40:20,294
Come forward
and join us!

848
01:40:22,235 --> 01:40:23,930
Or die!

849
01:40:29,475 --> 01:40:30,499
Draco.

850
01:40:36,182 --> 01:40:38,047
Draco.

851
01:40:40,954 --> 01:40:42,854
Draco.

852
01:40:45,692 --> 01:40:47,592
Come.

853
01:40:59,873 --> 01:41:02,000
Well done, Draco.

854
01:41:02,809 --> 01:41:04,674
Well done.

855
01:41:27,233 --> 01:41:29,997
Honestly, I expected something better.

856
01:41:34,407 --> 01:41:37,308
And who are you, young man?

857
01:41:38,578 --> 01:41:40,512
Neville Longbottom.

858
01:41:45,818 --> 01:41:49,515
Surely we can find you
a place in our ranks.

859
01:41:49,689 --> 01:41:51,919
I would like to say something.

860
01:41:58,064 --> 01:42:03,832
I'm sure we would all be fascinated
hear what you have to say.

861
01:42:06,839 --> 01:42:09,330
- It doesn't matter that Harry is no longer here.
- Shut up, Neville.

862
01:42:09,509 --> 01:42:12,103
People die every day.

863
01:42:13,780 --> 01:42:17,841
Friends, family.

864
01:42:19,886 --> 01:42:21,444
Yes.

865
01:42:22,889 --> 01:42:25,050
Tonight we lost Harry.

866
01:42:26,592 --> 01:42:31,086
But he is still with us, here.

867
01:42:32,098 --> 01:42:34,032
Also Fred...

868
01:42:35,034 --> 01:42:36,797
...and Remus.

869
01:42:37,904 --> 01:42:39,235
Tonks.

870
01:42:40,573 --> 01:42:42,473
All of them.

871
01:42:43,643 --> 01:42:45,907
They did not die in vain!

872
01:42:51,050 --> 01:42:52,108
But you do.

873
01:42:52,285 --> 01:42:54,651
Because you are wrong!

874
01:42:54,821 --> 01:42:57,813
Harry's heart was beating for everyone!
For all of us!

875
01:42:57,991 --> 01:42:59,583
This is not over!

876
01:43:03,696 --> 01:43:05,527
<i>Confringo!</i>

877
01:43:13,840 --> 01:43:15,398
Nope! Come back!

878
01:43:15,575 --> 01:43:19,511
Lucius! Come back!
Come back and fight!

879
01:43:19,679 --> 01:43:21,738
Come back!

880
01:43:26,786 --> 01:43:29,949
I'll lure him to the castle!
We must kill the snake!

881
01:43:30,123 --> 01:43:31,488
- You'll need this!
-Neville!

882
01:46:25,565 --> 01:46:28,090
Not my daughter, you bastard!

883
01:47:01,567 --> 01:47:02,898
You were right...

884
01:47:04,670 --> 01:47:07,002
...when you said that
your wand was failing you.

885
01:47:07,173 --> 01:47:08,834
It will always fail you!

886
01:47:10,142 --> 01:47:11,700
I killed Snape!

887
01:47:11,877 --> 01:47:14,004
What if the wand
Was it never Snape's?

888
01:47:14,180 --> 01:47:17,047
What if he was always loyal to another?

889
01:47:17,216 --> 01:47:20,413
Come on, Tom. Let's finish this
how we started it.

890
01:47:20,886 --> 01:47:21,910
Together!

891
01:50:56,402 --> 01:50:58,370
I thought you were going to be like him.

892
01:50:58,537 --> 01:51:02,906
I couldn't find my wand. Not the
I had lost in my entire life.

893
01:51:03,075 --> 01:51:05,066
I was in the folds
of my toga.

894
01:51:08,214 --> 01:51:10,011
Harry.

895
01:52:09,909 --> 01:52:13,606
Why wasn't it working for you?
the Elder Wand?

896
01:52:14,580 --> 01:52:16,514
I was responding to someone else.

897
01:52:17,483 --> 01:52:20,247
When he killed Snape,
He thought the wand would be his.

898
01:52:20,419 --> 01:52:24,583
But the wand never
It belonged to Snape.

899
01:52:24,757 --> 01:52:29,251
Draco disarmed Dumbledore
in the Astronomy Tower.

900
01:52:29,428 --> 01:52:33,455
From that moment on,
the wand responded to him.

901
01:52:34,333 --> 01:52:36,164
Until...

902
01:52:36,335 --> 01:52:40,897
...the other night, when I disarmed
to Draco at Malfoy Manor.

903
01:52:41,073 --> 01:52:43,200
That means...

904
01:52:44,743 --> 01:52:46,506
It's mine.

905
01:52:48,647 --> 01:52:49,909
What will we do with it?

906
01:52:50,349 --> 01:52:52,112
"Will we"?

907
01:52:52,518 --> 01:52:56,750
Just saying, it's the Elder Wand,
the most powerful in the world.

908
01:52:56,922 --> 01:53:00,858
With it we would be invincible.

909
01:54:28,514 --> 01:54:32,450
19 YEARS LATER

910
01:55:24,002 --> 01:55:25,663
Together.

911
01:55:42,988 --> 01:55:45,149
Take care!

912
01:56:04,343 --> 01:56:06,106
- Bag.
- Yes.

913
01:56:06,278 --> 01:56:07,336
Sweater.

914
01:56:09,014 --> 01:56:11,005
I'm going to miss you.

915
01:56:12,117 --> 01:56:13,846
Here they come.

916
01:56:29,034 --> 01:56:33,232
Dad? What if I
put in Slytherin?

917
01:56:35,507 --> 01:56:38,067
Albus Severus Potter...

918
01:56:39,344 --> 01:56:43,075
...we name you in honor
of two Hogwarts headmasters.

919
01:56:43,248 --> 01:56:44,840
One of them was from Slytherin.

920
01:56:45,017 --> 01:56:48,248
I have not met anyone braver.

921
01:56:50,122 --> 01:56:51,384
But suppose so.

922
01:56:51,557 --> 01:56:57,154
So Slytherin House
You will have acquired a wonderful wizard.

923
01:56:57,329 --> 01:57:03,029
But if you care so much,
you can choose Gryffindor.

924
01:57:03,202 --> 01:57:06,137
The Sorting Hat
take into account your wishes.

925
01:57:06,738 --> 01:57:07,898
Really?

926
01:57:08,073 --> 01:57:09,973
Really.

927
01:57:10,142 --> 01:57:12,804
- Goodbye, mom!
- Passengers on board!

928
01:57:12,978 --> 01:57:14,002
Ready?

929
01:57:14,179 --> 01:57:15,737
Ready.

930
01:57:27,993 --> 01:57:29,620
Come on, Jay, hurry up!

931
01:57:29,795 --> 01:57:31,353
Let's go now.

932
02:01:39,077 --> 02:01:41,671
HARRY POTTER AND THE HALLOWS
OF DEATH PART 2
